Headless service scripts: an entry that default-exports a function,
`export default async function main(cx)`, runs with an App and no window.

- A scope frame may have no window (scope::enter_headless). with_current and
  with_context refuse there, so window APIs throw "needs a live host call";
  everything App-only works.
- scheduler::Host keeps an optional window and resumes a headless task
  through the App; job drains skip nested-view flushing without a window.
- ShellRuntime::start_service(entry, policy, cx) loads the entry under the
  policy, calls main(cx) with the ambient AsyncContext as an owned task
  (rejections are logged) and returns a ServiceHandle, whose drop releases
  the application generation and cancels the policy's tasks, killing
  spawned process groups.
- ServiceWatcher restarts a service on a source change, dropping the old run
  before calling the host's start closure again. A failed start, the first
  one too, is logged and retried on the next save.
- HostModule::type_only names declared exports a module does not register,
  so variants of one module (a plugin's views and its service) can share one
  gpui-kit.d.ts that types them all.

